  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 25 actions (actions.js compileActionDefinitions, registered by init_actions) and 5 feedbacks (feedbacks.js compileFeedbackDefinitions, registered only when useTCP is true, else setFeedbackDefinitions({})).",
    "Protocol: OSC to Figure 53 Go Button, UDP by default, TCP when the config checkbox 'Use TCP?' is set (needed for feedbacks and variables). Config fields (config.js): Target IP (regex Regex.IP), Port (textinput, regex Regex.PORT, default '53100'), Use TCP? (default false), Use Tenths (default false, requires TCP), OSC Pascode.",
    "The descriptions of the actions name the OSC address the callback sends (actions.js sendCommand). The toggle actions additionally send a probe message when TCP is used. With UDP and TCP not ready the callback only logs.",
    "Cue and hit numbers are free text inputs without regex or useVariables; they are spliced into the OSC address unmodified. Feedback q_bg normalises the cue number with cleanCueNum (gobutton.js line 41: non-word characters other than '.' become '_').",
    "Feedback Status dropdowns use the numeric ids 1 (On) and 0 (Off) of choices.js ON_OFF (choices.js line 1), default 1. Callbacks use !!options.which: fs_bg compares self.fullScreen == !!which, mf_bg, dim_bg and mute_bg return the state && !!which, so choosing Off makes mf_bg, dim_bg and mute_bg never true (source behaviour).",
    "Variables and presets are not catalogued. The module sets instanceOptions.disableVariableValidation.",
    "The module is on @companion-module/base ^1.8.0 (1.x), so option values are not expressions. Not tested against Go Button or Companion."
  ]
